The Aggregate supply curve, shown with three ranges:

Keynesian range, in which prices are so low that companies would rather lower production than sell at a loss;
Intermediate range, in which an increase in price causes an increase in production;
Classical range, in which no more product can be produced no matter how high the price rises (because of full employment).
